The main function creates a `Character` object with 20 mana points available at the start of each battle. It then enters a loop where it calls the `selectAttack` and `regenerateMana` functions repeatedly, sleeping for one second between calls to simulate the passage of time. The `selectAttack` function will dynamically select an attack based on its cooldown period and mana requirements, while the `regenerateMana` function will regenerate the character's mana over time.

This code integrates seamlessly with the standardized attack interface provided by the game engine, while maintaining backward compatibility with existing attack handling mechanisms. Performance considerations have been taken into account to ensure that the function remains efficient even if called frequently in quick succession. Resource management has been optimized to minimize overhead, especially in high-frequency scenarios.']

