To ensure thread safety and avoid race conditions, this function must be integrated with an existing directory management system that supports concurrent access. A logging mechanism can also be implemented to track successful renamings and potential errors without affecting performance.

In terms of trade-offs between ease of use, maintainability, and scalability, this function provides a simple and straightforward way to rename files in a specified directory based on specific criteria while ensuring that no two files have the same name after renaming. It is also relatively efficient when processing directories with thousands of entries, but may need to be modified for larger or more complex file management tasks.

Documenting design choices and trade-offs will facilitate future enhancements and maintainability of this function.']

