The `ServiceManager` class provides methods for starting and stopping the service using a `ThreadPoolExecutor`. The implementation ensures that only two threads are active at any given time, and sets the maximum number of threads to four to minimize resource utilization.

6. Integration with Messaging Systems
----------------------------------

To integrate with an existing messaging system, the framework should provide a mechanism for sending messages when the service is stopped. This can be achieved using the messaging system's API or other suitable mechanisms.
