The function also implements efficient locking mechanisms to ensure thread safety without introducing significant overhead during peak times. Readers can access the hash table simultaneously without blocking writers, reducing contention among concurrent readers. Writers are responsible for acquiring a write lock before modifying the hash table or the array of structures, ensuring that only one writer is active at any given time and preventing concurrent modifications from corrupting the data structure.

