The function dynamically allocates memory for new trajectories as they are created and ensures that the total number of points across all trajectories does not exceed a given limit. It also checks for potential issues such as insufficient memory to allocate new points or to create new trajectories, and handles them accordingly.

The function provides a user-friendly API for initializing, manipulating, and retrieving trajectory data, while still maintaining efficient performance and scalability. It can be easily extended to support additional features such as trajectory filtering or summarization, and can seamlessly integrate with an existing logging system that records trajectory data at specific intervals.']

