public class CommandExecutor {
    private static final String LOG_FILE = "command-log.txt";

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Read properties file
        Properties props = new Properties();
        FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream("config.properties");
        props.load(fis);
        fis.close();

        // Get command and arguments from properties file
        String command = props.getProperty("command");
        List<String> args = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 1; i < args.length; i++) {
            args.add(props.getProperty("arg" + i));
        }

        // Check if target file exists, delete it if necessary
        File targetFile = new File(args.get(0));
        if (targetFile.exists()) {
            targetFile.delete();
        }

        // Create ProcessBuilder and set environment variables
        ProcessBuilder pb = new ProcessBuilder(command, args);
        pb.environment().put("VAR1", "value1");
        pb.environment().put("VAR2", "value2");

        // Set up stream readers for stdout and stderr
        BufferedReader stdoutReader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(pb.getInputStream()));
        BufferedReader stderrReader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(pb.getErrorStream()));

        // Start the process and read streams concurrently
        Process process = pb.start();
        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2);
        executor.submit(() -> {
            try (BufferedWriter writer = new BufferedWriter(new FileWriter(LOG_FILE))) {
                String line;
                while ((line = stdoutReader.readLine()) != null) {
                    writer.write(line + "\n");
                }
            } catch (IOException e) {
                // Handle exception
            }
        });
        executor.submit(() -> {
            try (BufferedWriter writer = new BufferedWriter(new FileWriter(LOG_FILE))) {
                String line;
                while ((line = stderrReader.readLine()) != null) {
                    writer.write(line + "\n");
                }
            } catch (IOException e) {
                // Handle exception
            }
        });

        // Wait for process to finish and log end time
        try {
            process.waitFor();
            long endTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
            writer.write("Process finished with exit code " + process.exitValue());
            writer.write("Total execution time: " + (endTime - startTime) + "ms");
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            // Handle exception
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses the `ProcessBuilder` class to execute a command with multiple arguments, and sets environment variables for the executed process. It also checks if the target file exists before starting the command, and deletes it if necessary. The program reads both standard output and error streams concurrently using `BufferedReader`, and logs the entire execution process into a specified log file.

The code uses a thread pool to read the streams concurrently, which helps improve performance by processing multiple streams simultaneously. It also provides detailed status reports on command execution, including any errors, and allows configuration through an external properties file. Developers can evaluate and implement caching strategies to optimize repeated command executions, considering trade-offs between cache hit rates and memory consumption.

