To handle a high volume of concurrent read and write operations without degradation in performance or resource exhaustion, the class uses appropriate synchronization techniques to prevent race conditions and ensure thread safety. The cache is designed to be scalable, leveraging distributed caching services effectively and minimizing the impact of scaling on performance.

The system is also optimized for low-latency access to frequently requested product metadata, balancing between local caching and remote data retrieval to maintain optimal performance under varying load conditions. Additionally, the class uses in-memory storage to ensure resilience against unexpected system restarts.

