To ensure that the function manages memory efficiently to avoid leaks, it considers scenarios where the size of the offset and key arrays may vary at runtime. It allocates memory for the arrays using `malloc()` and initializes them to zero using `memset()`. This helps to prevent memory leaks in case the size of the array is not known at compile time.

