After creating all the threads, the function joins them using the `pthread_join` function. If any of the threads fails with an error code, the function prints an error message and frees the memory allocated for the profiles.

The function then validates the generated profiles against predefined criteria using the external configuration management library. It checks if each identifier is within the allowed range, unique, and follows a specific distribution. If any of these criteria are not met, the function prints an error message and frees the memory allocated for the profiles.

Finally, the function free's the memory for the identifier, numerical value, and preference text description arrays, and returns the generated profiles.

