The code includes functions for adding new users to the system, deleting users from the system, inserting log entries into the system, deleting log entries from the system, querying log entries based on user ID or time range, and initializing the logging system. The functions are thread-safe and use synchronization mechanisms such as a mutex and a semaphore to ensure data consistency and integrity.

The code also includes an external logging library for validating the integrity of each log entry against predefined criteria before committing it to storage. This library can be used to check the format of log entries, their authenticity, and other relevant factors.

To handle large volumes of log data efficiently, the system uses dynamic resizing strategies that optimize performance and memory usage. The system also supports flexible configuration changes during runtime, allowing for the addition or removal of users and their associated actions.']

